**Phase 2: Rigorous Validation (T.R.U.S.T.):** We'll immediately run that draft through the 5-step T.R.U.S.T. protocol to make it accurate, safe, and ready to publish.

**Step 1: Define the Task**
&nbsp;  

**• Goal:** Summarize a new data retention policy for internal staff.
&nbsp;  

**• Source Document:** We'll use the following (fictional) policy text.

&nbsp;  

**Alberta Public Sector Data Retention Policy Update (2025)**

&nbsp;  

Effective January 1, 2026, all public sector employees must retain email communications related to policy decisions for a minimum of seven years, up from the previous requirement of five years. This change aligns with new Access to Information Act (“ATI Act”) and the Protection of Privacy Act (“PPA”). Employees should archive emails using the approved IT system (GovArchive) by the end of each quarter. Non-compliance may result in disciplinary action. For questions, contact the Records Management Office at records@gov.ab.ca.

